rs, the other lists corresponding fill colors.\n 281: \n 282:     Rule:\n 283:     - Locate the palette legend on a grid edge and read it as a border→fill color mapping.\n 284:     - Find enclosed bg regions (holes) inside sprites that don't touch the grid boundary.\n 285:     - For each hole, identify the most common adjacent border color, look it up in the palette, and fill the hole with the mapped fill color.\n 286: \n 287:     Key insight: The palette's edge position and orientation determine reading direction; border colors in the palette uniquely key into fill colors.\n 288:     \"\"\"\n 289:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n 290:     bg = _bg_boundary(g)\n 291: \n 292:     mapping, pal_mask = _palette_mapping(g, bg)\n 293:     assert mapping, \"main: palette mapping must be non-empty\"\n 294: \n 295:     out = g.copy()\n 296:     _fill_enclosed_bg_regions(out, bg, mapping, pal_mask)\n 297: \n 298:     return out\n 299: \n 300: # --------------- generator (c) ---------------\n 301: \n 302: # -- Configuration constants --------------------------------------------------\n 303: # Grid dimensions\n 304: _GRID_H_MIN, _GRID_H_MAX = 4, 13\n 305: _GRID_W_MIN, _GRID_W_MAX = 10, 15\n 306: _SMALL_H_THRESHOLD = 6        # below this, prefer left/right palette\n 307: _SMALL_H_PALETTE_FLIP = 0.7   # probability of flipping top/bottom -> left/right\n 308: _TINY_H_THRESHOLD = 5         # below this, cap sprite height at 3\n 309: \n 310: # Palette\n 311: _PALETTE_N_MIN, _PALETTE_N_MAX = 2, 5\n 312: \n 313: # Sprite geometry\n 314: _SPRITE_H_MAX = 7\n 315: _SPRITE_W_MAX = 6\n 316: _SPRITE_DIM_SUM_CAP = 10      # if sh + sw exceeds this, clamp sw\n 317: _SPRITE_CELL_MAX = 16\n 318: _FILLED_SPRITE_MAX = 3\n 319: \n 320: # Sprite mutation probabilities\n 321: _P_HORIZ_WALL = 0.3           # add horizontal internal wall\n 322: _P_VERT_WALL = 0.3            # add vertical internal wall\n 323: _P_BORDER_REMOVAL = 0.4       # remove border cells for irregular shapes\n 324: _P_DIAM